{"kind":"assert","text":"Version decision and order, after the 0.4.0 signing.\n\n1. Version. By ruling `163de663`, the head of E4, A1 and CR-2 opens\n   the next minor version of each application whose identifiers its\n   source changes. Lending and Counter become 0.5.0. Apply the same\n   rule to Grow if its identifiers change, and tell me the numbers.\n   0.5.0 stays open. I sign it when a room needs it.\n2. Order of heads:\n   a. LS-5 with LC-4 (`0e91ee10`, the request after this act). One\n      gate, then the smoke run on a `diag/` branch at the gated\n      head, then the review.\n   b. E4, A1 and CR-2 on the main that holds head a. `npm run pins`,\n      one full gate, the review, the landing.\n   c. AE-1 with the caps of `790afe00`.\n   d. C4 with E4-B.\n3. AE-1 can join head a if its source is independent of LS-5 and\n   you judge one review scope readable. Tell me before the gate.\n4. After head b lands and deploys, I create the room\n   `counter-witness` and the new Lending room, and I install the\n   0.4.0 releases there. Those installs need the trust rows of LC-4\n   and the route of CR-2.\n5. Each head changes Worker bundles. I deploy after each landing\n   check, with one act to you before the deployment.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}